curved|bent|ADJECTIVE|bending rather than straight|Having a shape that bends smoothly rather than staying straight.|cong|The curved handle fitted comfortably in her hand.|Tay cầm cong nằm vừa vặn, thoải mái trong tay cô ấy.|Can describe an edge, line or surface; curved does not necessarily mean circular.|curved
grasp|hold-firmly|VERB|hold firmly|To take and hold something firmly with your hand.|nắm chặt|He grasped the ladder with both hands before climbing.|Anh ấy nắm chặt thang bằng cả hai tay trước khi leo.|Transitive; grasp something. The physical object is the direct object.|grasp
grasp|understand|VERB|understand an idea|To understand an idea, fact or situation.|hiểu, nắm bắt|It took me several readings to grasp the argument.|Tôi phải đọc vài lần mới hiểu được lập luận.|Transitive; grasp an idea or grasp how something works.|grasp
grasp|physical-hold|NOUN|firm hold|A firm hold on someone or something, usually with a hand.|cái nắm, sự nắm giữ|The handle slipped from his grasp when the boat rocked.|Tay cầm tuột khỏi tay anh ấy khi thuyền chao đảo.|Usually singular; a grasp on something or from someone's grasp.|grasp
grasp|understanding|NOUN|understanding of a subject|A person's understanding of a subject or situation.|sự hiểu biết, khả năng nắm bắt|Her clear grasp of the rules helped the new players.|Sự hiểu biết rõ ràng của cô ấy về luật chơi giúp những người chơi mới.|Usually singular; a good or clear grasp of something.|grasp
reply|answer|VERB|give an answer|To answer someone who has spoken or sent a message.|trả lời|The curator replied to my question about the painting.|Người phụ trách bảo tàng trả lời câu hỏi của tôi về bức tranh.|Reply to someone or something; reply that can introduce the answer's content.|reply
reply|response|NOUN|answer given|An answer given to a question, remark or message.|câu trả lời, lời hồi đáp|His brief reply confirmed that the parcel had arrived.|Lời hồi đáp ngắn của anh ấy xác nhận rằng bưu kiện đã đến.|Countable; a reply to a message or question.|reply
certain|sure|ADJECTIVE|without doubt|Having no doubt that something is true or will happen.|chắc chắn, tin chắc|She was certain that she had left the keys in her coat.|Cô ấy tin chắc rằng mình đã để chìa khóa trong áo khoác.|Certain that plus clause or certain about something; certainty is a belief, not proof.|certain
certain|particular-unspecified|ADJECTIVE|particular but unspecified|Used to refer to particular people or things without stating exactly which ones.|một số, nhất định|Certain seats are reserved for passengers with mobility difficulties.|Một số ghế được dành cho hành khách gặp khó khăn khi di chuyển.|Before a plural noun or in a certain plus singular noun; not used after be in this sense.|certain
paralysis|loss-of-movement|NOUN|inability to move|A condition in which someone cannot move some or all of their body.|sự liệt, tê liệt|The article describes how paralysis affected movement in his left arm.|Bài báo mô tả tình trạng liệt đã ảnh hưởng đến cử động ở cánh tay trái của anh ấy như thế nào.|Usually uncountable; paralysis of a body part. The word does not specify its cause.|paralysis
trial|court-hearing|NOUN|court examination|A formal examination of evidence in court to decide a legal case.|phiên tòa, việc xét xử|Several witnesses gave evidence during the trial.|Một số nhân chứng cung cấp lời khai trong phiên tòa.|Countable; on trial for an offence. This word does not specify a particular legal procedure.|trial
trial|test|NOUN|test of performance|A test used to find out how well something works or what effects it has.|cuộc thử nghiệm|The hospital announced a trial of a new monitoring device.|Bệnh viện công bố một cuộc thử nghiệm thiết bị theo dõi mới.|Countable; a trial of something or a clinical trial. A trial does not imply a successful result.|trial
earthquake|ground-shaking|NOUN|sudden ground shaking|A sudden movement that makes the ground shake.|trận động đất|A small earthquake rattled the cups on the shelf.|Một trận động đất nhỏ làm những chiếc cốc trên kệ rung lên.|Countable; an earthquake may be small and need not cause major damage.|earthquake
marine|sea-related|ADJECTIVE|connected with the sea|Connected with the sea or with organisms that live in it.|thuộc biển, sống ở biển|The students photographed marine life around the reef.|Các học sinh chụp ảnh sinh vật biển quanh rạn san hô.|Often before nouns such as life, plants or environment; this record proposes only the adjective.|marine
diary|personal-record|NOUN|personal written record|A book or other record where someone writes about their experiences, thoughts and feelings.|nhật ký|During the journey, she kept a diary of the people she met.|Trong chuyến đi, cô ấy viết nhật ký về những người mình gặp.|Countable; keep or write a diary. Entries are often organized by date.|diary
diary|appointment-book|NOUN|appointment record|A book or record used to note appointments and planned events.|sổ lịch hẹn|He checked his diary before agreeing to a meeting on Thursday.|Anh ấy xem sổ lịch hẹn trước khi đồng ý họp vào thứ Năm.|Countable; put an appointment in a diary. This sense is common in British English.|diary
discipline|rule-following|NOUN|control through rules|Training or control that helps people follow rules and behave in an orderly way.|kỷ luật|The head teacher discussed classroom discipline with the new staff.|Hiệu trưởng thảo luận về kỷ luật trong lớp học với các nhân viên mới.|Usually uncountable; classroom discipline or maintain discipline.|discipline
discipline|self-control|NOUN|controlled effort|The ability to control your actions and continue working towards a goal.|tính kỷ luật, khả năng tự kiểm soát|Daily practice required more discipline than she had expected.|Việc luyện tập hằng ngày đòi hỏi tính kỷ luật cao hơn cô ấy từng nghĩ.|Usually uncountable; discipline to do something or self-discipline.|discipline
discipline|subject|NOUN|field of study|A particular branch of academic knowledge or study.|ngành học, lĩnh vực học thuật|The course brings together students from several disciplines.|Khóa học tập hợp sinh viên từ nhiều ngành học.|Countable; an academic discipline. Distinct from rule-following or self-control.|discipline
scribe|manuscript-copyist|NOUN|historical writer and copyist|Someone whose job, especially before printing was common, was to copy texts or record information by hand.|người chép bản thảo, người ghi chép|The scribe copied the agreement onto a fresh sheet of parchment.|Người ghi chép chép bản thỏa thuận lên một tờ da mới.|Countable; often used for a historical occupation.|scribe
transparent|see-through|ADJECTIVE|clear enough to see through|Allowing objects on the other side to be seen clearly.|trong suốt|The transparent container made it easy to see the seeds inside.|Chiếc hộp trong suốt giúp dễ dàng nhìn thấy hạt giống bên trong.|Transparent differs from translucent, which admits light without a clear view.|transparent
transparent|open-process|ADJECTIVE|open to inspection|Open and clear about how decisions are made or activities are carried out.|minh bạch|A transparent budget shows how each donation is spent.|Một ngân sách minh bạch cho thấy từng khoản quyên góp được sử dụng như thế nào.|Can describe an organization or process; transparency does not itself guarantee fairness.|transparent
proceeds|money-received|NOUN|money received|Money obtained from selling something or holding an event.|số tiền thu được|The proceeds from the pottery sale paid for new workshop tools.|Tiền bán đồ gốm được dùng để mua dụng cụ mới cho xưởng.|Plural noun: proceeds are. Net proceeds specifies money remaining after costs.|proceeds
farewell|goodbye|NOUN|act of saying goodbye|Words or an occasion through which someone says goodbye.|lời từ biệt, việc chia tay|They exchanged a warm farewell at the station.|Họ trao nhau lời từ biệt ấm áp ở nhà ga.|Countable for a particular goodbye; say or bid farewell to someone.|farewell
biodiversity|variety-of-life|NOUN|variety of living organisms|The range of different living organisms found in an area or across the world.|sự đa dạng sinh học|The school garden supports biodiversity by providing several kinds of habitat.|Khu vườn trường hỗ trợ sự đa dạng sinh học bằng cách tạo ra nhiều kiểu môi trường sống.|Uncountable; can describe local or global variety. It is not limited to large animals and plants.|biodiversity
storm|severe-weather|NOUN|severe weather event|A period of severe weather, often involving strong winds, heavy rain or snow.|cơn bão|The ferry stayed in the harbour until the storm passed.|Phà ở lại bến cảng cho đến khi cơn bão qua đi.|Countable; a storm need not be a tropical cyclone. This record does not propose a verb.|storm
native|first-language|ADJECTIVE|first language|Describing the language a person first learns in early life.|bản ngữ, mẹ đẻ|She writes poetry in her native language as well as in English.|Cô ấy viết thơ bằng tiếng mẹ đẻ của mình và cả bằng tiếng Anh.|Used in native language or native speaker; it does not identify a person's nationality.|native
native|indigenous-to-place|ADJECTIVE|naturally originating there|Originating or growing naturally in a particular place rather than being introduced from elsewhere.|bản địa|This fern is native to the mountain forests of the region.|Loài dương xỉ này có nguồn gốc tự nhiên từ các khu rừng núi trong vùng.|Native to a place; a native plant is one that originates naturally there.|native
native|person-born-there|NOUN|person born in a place|Someone who was born in a particular town, region or country.|người gốc, người sinh ra ở|A native of the coastal town, he knew its narrow streets well.|Là người sinh ra ở thị trấn ven biển đó, anh ấy hiểu rõ những con phố hẹp nơi đây.|Countable; prefer a native of a named place. Using natives as a general label for peoples can be disrespectful.|native
addiction|compulsive-dependence|NOUN|hard-to-control dependence|A strong dependence on a substance or activity that is difficult to stop despite harmful effects.|chứng nghiện, sự nghiện|The memoir describes her struggle with gambling addiction.|Cuốn hồi ký mô tả cuộc đấu tranh của cô ấy với chứng nghiện cờ bạc.|Addiction to something; not simply enjoyment or a strong interest. This record does not diagnose anyone.|addiction
election|vote|NOUN|selection by voting|An organized process in which people vote to choose a representative or office holder.|cuộc bầu cử|The members held an election to choose their new chairperson.|Các thành viên tổ chức một cuộc bầu cử để chọn chủ tịch mới.|Countable; hold an election or vote in an election.|election
highly|great-degree|ADVERB|to a great degree|To a very great extent or degree.|rất, ở mức độ cao|The workshop was highly useful to the new instructors.|Buổi tập huấn rất hữu ích đối với những người hướng dẫn mới.|Often modifies adjectives or participles, as in highly skilled or highly successful.|highly
